events.handlers.docs:
bunny_upload is a caddyevents.Handler that, whenever Caddy obtains or
renews a certificate, uploads that certificate to a Bunny.net Pull Zone
as a custom certificate.

It works by reading the newly-stored certificate/key pair straight out
of Caddy's own certificate storage (whatever "storage" module Caddy is
configured to use), so it doesn't care which issuer (Let's Encrypt,
ZeroSSL, internal CA, etc.) produced it.

Example Caddyfile (as a global "events" subscription):

	{
		events {
			on cert_obtained bunny_upload {$BUNNY_API_KEY} {
				domains cdn.example.com static.example.com
			}
			on cert_renewed bunny_upload {$BUNNY_API_KEY} {
				domains cdn.example.com static.example.com
			}
		}
	}

Example JSON:

	{
		"apps": {
			"events": {
				"subscriptions": [
					{
						"events": ["cert_obtained", "cert_renewed"],
						"handlers": [
							{
								"handler": "bunny_upload",
								"api_key": "{env.BUNNY_API_KEY}",
								"domains": ["cdn.example.com"]
							}
						]
					}
				]
			}
		}
	}
